# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data (raw archive hours, live poll samples — regenerable, often large).
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `data/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, so a future `docs/data/` or `tests/data/` would be ignored by
# a rule written about this one — silently, which is the only way ignore rules
# ever go wrong.
/data/

# OS / editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Transformation build artifacts (compiled SQL, run results, package installs)
dbt/target/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/logs/
dbt/.user.yml

# Logs
*.log
# ...except this one, and the exception is load-bearing rather than tidy.
# `aggregates/runs.log` is the scheduled job's run record: on a day the job
# produces no data it is the ONLY evidence the job ran at all, and committing it
# is also what stops a public repository's scheduled workflow being disabled after
# 60 days of no activity. `*.log` above swallowed it — so the job would have run
# green, staged nothing, committed nothing, reported success, and been switched
# off mid-absence with no error anywhere. Caught by `git check-ignore`, not by
# reading this file. See tests/test_committed_paths.py, which asserts it.
!/aggregates/runs.log
